<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a multiplication grid</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Baraka expanded \((x + {@b@})^3\) by multiplication. His working has one mistake.</p><p>Line 1: \((x + {@b@})^3 = (x + {@b@})^2(x + {@b@})\)</p><p>Line 2: \((x + {@b@})^2 = {@sqd@}\)</p><p>Line 3: he multiplied the terms of line 2 by \(x\) and by \({@b@}\) in a grid:</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\times\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(x^2\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@m2x@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b2@}\)</th></tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(x\)</th><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@c[1]@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@c[2]@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@c[3]@}\)</td></tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b@}\)</th><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@c[4]@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@c[5]@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@c[6]@}\)</td></tr></table><p>Line 4: So \((x + {@b@})^3 = {@bar@}\)</p><p>(a) Which line has the mistake?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Write the correct expansion of \((x + {@b@})^3\).</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A cube is the square multiplied by one more bracket. Check each line: the square must have the middle term \(2 \times {@b@} \times x\), each cell must be the product of its row and its column, and like terms must be added.</p>[[if test="is(er=1)"]]<p>(a) The mistake is in Line 2. Baraka left out the 2 in the middle term: \((x + {@b@})^2 = {@sq@}\).</p>[[elif test="is(er=2)"]]<p>(a) The mistake is in Line 3. In the bottom row, \({@b@} \times {@t2@}\) is \({@b*t2@}\), not \({@c[5]@}\): both factors must be multiplied.</p>[[else]]<p>(a) The mistake is in Line 4. The grid is right, but there are two terms in \(x\) to add, \({@b^2*x@}\) and \({@2*b^2*x@}\), giving \({@3*b^2*x@}\).</p>[[/if]]<p>(b) The correct working is \((x + {@b@})^2 = {@sq@}\), then</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\times\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@x^2@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@t2@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b2@}\)</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@x@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(x^2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(t2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(b2)@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(x^2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(t2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(b2)@}\)</td></tr></table><p>so \((x + {@b@})^3 = {@ta@}\). Check: \(x = 1\) gives \({@b1@}^3 = {@chk@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
